Z||000000||NOS3800||08-23-2001||06:49 PM||||High Performance magazine is again asking for cars to be included in a shootout at E-town raceway in NJ. They have stated that clubs can be included, meaning it can be ALL fieros, no matter how fast! Go to this link, fill out the forms under HPP shootout and then mail to me.Go to this link if you want to be included in the HPP pontiac shootout.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.pontiacsouthernnationals.com/HPP_Shootout.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pontiacsouthernnationals.com/HPP_Shootout.htm</A> <P>We CAN do this as a club, PLEASE send me the info they need so I can get a package together!<BR>Send to:<BR>Bill Sessions<BR>4824 Kingfisher Court<BR>Waldorf MD. 20603<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-23-2001||06:54 PM||||Bill,<BR>When are you going to mail them all in...I want to finish my car...paint/interior.   Plus I have to break in my 3400.<P>Hmm...maybe on the "HPP Shootout dislikes" line we all should put "No Fieros"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks<BR>Joe<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||NOS3800||08-23-2001||07:05 PM||||Just send me what you got with a disclaimer stating where the car will be at in say two months. I am sure they won't do the shootout until the winter at the earliest. I have NEVER seen a Fiero in any orf their shootouts, so it would be a new experience for them, and us for that matter!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||10
